    "number": 36376,
    "state": "open",
    "state_reason": null,
    "title": "Add rare BIP324 decoy packets for protocol compatibility enforcement",
    "body": "BIP324 supports decoy packets as a means for traffic shaping. That feature isn't used (we never send them, but support receiving them), and might never be, but not using it risks having other P2P clients not supporting it at all.\n\nTherefore I suggest that every V2 connection occasionally is sent a decoy packet, even a tiny one, just to make sure support isn't silently missing from other software.",
